WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
Your pancreas makes enzymes
that digest protein,

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.590
and sends them out of its cells.

3
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:11.070
In the 1960s, George Palade's group
tracked that export in pancreas cells.

4
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.810
They fed the cells radioactive amino
acids for a few minutes: the pulse.

5
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.470
Then plain ones: the chase.

6
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.150
At each time point, they asked:
where is the radioactive protein now?

7
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.050
So how does the pancreas ship
out enzymes that digest protein,

8
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.190
without digesting itself?

9
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.280
In this mission, you'll follow that
radioactive protein through the cell,

10
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.740
minute by minute.

11
00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.300
Then you'll see how many proteins
are finished before they work,

12
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.580
some with added sugar chains.

13
00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:45.670
Your mission: find out how the pancreas
ships out protein-digesting enzymes,

14
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.800
yet never digests itself.
